==Enemy==
A Dark variant of [[Le'boin]]. He has slightly more range, less speed and far higher stats, with unusually high health compared to enemies of the same caliber.

==Strategy==
Le'noir is more tank oriented than Le'boin, as the latter is often seen at extremely high buffs reaching up to 50k damage. Compared to a 10,000% Le'boin, a 200% Le'noir has more than double the health, but a little less than half the damage.

Le'noir's range increase still doesn't allow him to hit backliners easily, so the likes of [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun]] and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut]] can deal with him in company of meatshields given enough time.

Le'noir's long time between attacks makes him particularly vulnerable to stunlocking by [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] if such an opening is present, as his singular knockback prevents him from repositioning. One more strategy is using [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic King Dragon]] and other Backliner-class Units as his [[True Form]] gives him enough range to effectively chip away at Le'noir; a well timed [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] can also at least hit Le'noir once, doing massive damage to him provided good conditions, further augmented by his wave attack talent which allows him to reach Le'noir even if other enemies get in the way. Other [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance]]/[[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave]]/[[:Category:Surge Attack Cats|Surge]] attackers may also see use against Le'noir, as they will be able to consistently chip him.

